Use the declared payload length for the Rust ADT property's slice metadata.

The DST metadata describes value[], excluding the property header. Read the
complete little-endian u32 length instead of adding a Rust char-array header
size to its first byte. ADT bit 31 is a template marker, not payload length;
normalize every Rust payload-length use through the existing format mask while
leaving the wire field unchanged. Construct a raw slice pointer without a
temporary reference. Physical ADT buffer bounds remain the caller's existing
contract.

